cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the method it implements, given under
  preferred-citation, and for USRCAT the article under references.
type: software
title: "USR: Ultrafast Shape Recognition"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of Ultrafast Shape Recognition (USR) and of USRCAT,
  USR with CREDO atom types, on top of RDKit. USR describes the shape of a 3D
  conformer with 12 moments of its atomic distance distributions and compares
  shapes without aligning them; USRCAT adds 48 moments of its hydrophobic,
  aromatic, hydrogen-bond acceptor and donor atoms. The package calculates the
  moments from SD files or RDKit molecules and screens a database of moments
  against query molecules, from Python or the `usr` and `usrcat` command
  lines.
authors:
